                                                "sense_id": "772cadee-4488-3cf7-aa2d-b5833880535a",
                                                "text": "The effect of a reduced collision rate at large orbital radii on the formation timescale of planets is possibly explained by Alexander (2012) who suggests that circumbinary planets have more time to form than planets around single stars."
